# Assumptions and limitations

This file lists the definitions, data handling, judgement calls and limits behind
the analysis. Every number here comes from the executed SQL files and notebooks.

---

## 1. Definitions

| Term | Definition |
|---|---|
| Revenue | In-app purchase revenue (`purchase.usd_amount`) only. Ad revenue is not in the extract. `reward_amount` is in-game currency given away, a cost to the game economy, never revenue. |
| Gross revenue | Positive rows of `purchase_clean` (duplicates removed, refunds excluded), dated by purchase date. Total **$217,593.22**. Used for ARPDAU and all per-player work. |
| Net revenue | Gross + refunds = **$214,343.48**. Reported in totals only, because refunds land days after the purchase they reverse. |
| Active player-day / DAU | One row in `player_day`. |
| ARPDAU | Gross revenue ÷ active player-days. For a period: total ÷ total, never an average of daily ratios. |
| Daily payer share | Buyers who were also active that day ÷ DAU. |
| Retention Dn | Share of an install cohort active on exactly install date + n. Cohorts: installs 1 Jan – 30 Apr 2026. |
| Country tier | `country_tier` from the profile (1 = highest revenue potential). |
| First 30 / last 30 days | 1–30 Jan vs 1–30 Apr (Part 2a). Both contain 4 sale days. |
| Value per install | Gross IAP in the first 30 or 60 days after install, per install (Jan–Mar installs for 30 days, Jan–Feb for 60 days). |
| 14-day lapse | A player active at least once in the 7 days up to a weekly snapshot, with no activity in the 14 days after it. |

