## 2. Who is in which analysis

Different questions need different populations. This is the main source of
"wrong but plausible" numbers in this extract, so it is shown explicitly.

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    ALL[All 80,295 players in the extract]
    ALL --> PRE[16,000 installed May–Dec 2025<br/>99.4% active in 2026 → survivors]
    ALL --> NEW[64,295 installed 1 Jan – 30 Apr 2026]

    PRE --> BASE[Active base<br/>DAU · ARPDAU · payer share · Part 2a · lapse model]
    NEW --> BASE

    NEW --> COH[Install cohorts]
    COH --> R[Retention grid<br/>cell shown only if every player has reached day n]
    COH --> Q[Jan–Mar installs<br/>full 30 days observed]
    Q --> CH[Part 3 channels · time to first purchase · 30-day value]
    Q --> Q60[Jan–Feb installs<br/>60-day value]

    ALL --> X[36 anomalous currency accounts]
    X -. excluded .-> LM[lapse model]
```

Pre-window players stay in the active base because they are genuinely active
players. They are kept out of anything anchored on install date, because only
the ones who were still playing in 2026 appear in the extract.

