## 3. Data quality: what was found and how it was handled

| Issue | Evidence | Handling |
|---|---|---|
| `ad_view` timestamps are 8 hours ahead | Ad events span 14:00–07:59 with none 08:00–13:59, while purchases and spends span 06:00–23:59. Raw: 51% of ad player-days have no activity row that day; shifted −8h: 0%. Raw: 8,212 player-days change cap mid-day; shifted: 0. | All ad analysis uses `ad_view_local`. The 7,732 events dated 1 May on the raw clock are 30 April events and are kept. |
| Ad data missing 5–6 March | No ad rows on either day; activity, purchases and currency spends are normal. | Treated as a logging gap: excluded from ad trends, not counted as zero. |
| Duplicate purchases | 122 `purchase_id`s appear twice with the same device, pack and amount, hours apart on the same day. | First occurrence kept in `purchase_clean` (−$1,815.82). |
| Refunds | 226 negative rows after de-duplication (−$3,249.74); 222 match an earlier purchase of the same pack by the same player. | Excluded from gross revenue, included in net. |
| Pre-window players are survivors | 16,000 players installed May–Dec 2025; 99.4% are active in 2026. | Excluded from install-based analysis (section 2). |
| Purchases on days with no activity row | 2,449 of 15,078 gross purchases (16.2%, $35,732.51). The share is flat across hours and tiers, so it is not a timezone effect. | Revenue kept. Daily payer share counts only buyers active that day. |
| Purchases before `install_date` | 111 purchases by 110 players, a few days before install. | Players kept; time to first purchase clipped to day 0. |
| `original_device_id` links | 3,211 links: 94% cross countries, 42% cross platforms, one device links to itself. | Not used; each `device_id` is one player. |
| Anomalous currency spends | 36 accounts spend up to 75.8M in one event, against balances that never exceed ~17k. | Excluded from the lapse model. No effect on IAP revenue. |
| Refund rows keep `sale_flag` | Refunds of sale purchases carry `sale_flag = 1` on non-sale days. | Sale days identified from positive purchases only. |
| First activity after install | Only ~65% of new installs are active on their install date; the rest first appear 1–14 days later. | Retention stays anchored on `install_date` (the brief's definition); D1 is read with this in mind. |
| Empty CSV fields | A plain MySQL `LOAD DATA` turns empty fields into `0` / `0000-00-00`. | `setup.sql` loads them as `NULL`. |

